# FalconPulsar QuickDock icon set — ONE source of truth for both platforms.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# macOS drew its menu icons with SF Symbols; Windows drew them with Segoe
# MDL2 Assets. Two different platform fonts, so the two menus could never
# agree: `brain`, `square.grid.2x2` and `safari` have no MDL2 equivalent at
# all, and SF Symbols cannot be licensed or shipped on Windows. There is no
# setting that makes font A look like font B.
#
# It also made every icon change unverifiable from a Mac. Swapping Stop's
# drawn square for MDL2 E71A was reverted precisely because nobody here can
# render Segoe MDL2 to check, and a glyph that resolves to a blank box costs
# the item its icon entirely.
#
# Owning the geometry fixes both: the two platforms are identical BY
# CONSTRUCTION, and the shapes can be rasterized and looked at before they
# ship.
#
# FORMAT
#
#   <name> | <mode> | <path data>
#
# One icon may span several lines; they are drawn in order, so a filled
# backdrop can precede a knocked-out stroke.
#
#   mode  F      fill the subpath (non-zero winding)
#         S<w>   stroke it, width <w> in grid units, round cap + round join
#         K      fill in the KNOCKOUT colour (the menu background) — used for
#                the arrow inside a filled circle, so one icon reads as two
#                tones without needing a second colour channel
#
# Path commands are ABSOLUTE ONLY and limited to four, which is the whole
# grammar both renderers must implement:
#
#   M x y                    move to
#   L x y                    line to
#   C x1 y1 x2 y2 x y        cubic bezier
#   Z                        close subpath
#
# No arcs. A circle is four cubics — exact enough at 16px and it keeps both
# parsers to about sixty lines each, which is the point.
#
# GRID
#
# 24x24, origin top-left, y increasing downward (matches both GDI+ and the
# flipped NSGraphicsContext the macOS renderer sets up). Live area is inset
# to roughly 3..21 so a 2-unit stroke never clips at the bounding box.
#
# Circle constant: a 12-radius circle centred at (12,12) uses control-point
# offset 12 * 0.5523 = 6.63.
#
# EDITING
#
# Change this file, run `scripts/sync-icons.sh`, and BOTH platforms update.
# CI runs `scripts/sync-icons.sh --check` and fails if the generated files
# have drifted, the same guard `sync-version.sh` provides for VERSION.
# `scripts/preview-icons.swift` renders a contact sheet — look at it before
# committing. That is the whole reason this indirection is worth having.

# ── Open FalconPulsar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A globe: the Web UI opens in a browser. macOS used `safari`, a compass,
# which is a Safari-specific mark and reads as nothing on Windows. A globe
# carries the same "this opens on the web" meaning on both.
globe | S2 | M 12 3.2 C 16.86 3.2 20.8 7.14 20.8 12 C 20.8 16.86 16.86 20.8 12 20.8 C 7.14 20.8 3.2 16.86 3.2 12 C 3.2 7.14 7.14 3.2 12 3.2 Z
globe | S2 | M 3.4 12 L 20.6 12
globe | S2 | M 12 3.2 C 14.6 6 15.6 9 15.6 12 C 15.6 15 14.6 18 12 20.8 C 9.4 18 8.4 15 8.4 12 C 8.4 9 9.4 6 12 3.2 Z

# ── Open AI Engine ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A node graph, not a brain.
#
# macOS used SF Symbols' `brain`, and the drawn version of it failed the only
# test that matters: at 14-16px — the size these actually ship at — a brain's
# lobes and folds are about one grid unit, under a pixel, so they vanish and
# leave a circle with a line down it. Redrawing it coarser was tried and
# rendered; it still read as a circle. SF Symbols has the same problem, so
# macOS was never crisp here either.
#
# Worse, "Open FalconPulsar" sits directly above with a GLOBE — also a circle.
# Two adjacent circles in the same menu.
#
# Three connected nodes survive 16px (distinct filled dots, nothing thinner
# than the stroke), read as nothing else in the set, and say what the Engine
# actually is: the surface where agent flows are authored, simulated and
# deployed. The shell embeds it as "Agents" mode, hence the name.
agents | S2.6 | M 6.5 6.5 L 16 11.5
agents | S2.6 | M 6.5 6.5 L 9.5 17
agents | S2.6 | M 16 11.5 L 9.5 17
agents | F | M 6.5 2.6 C 8.65 2.6 10.4 4.35 10.4 6.5 C 10.4 8.65 8.65 10.4 6.5 10.4 C 4.35 10.4 2.6 8.65 2.6 6.5 C 2.6 4.35 4.35 2.6 6.5 2.6 Z
agents | F | M 17.8 7.9 C 19.79 7.9 21.4 9.51 21.4 11.5 C 21.4 13.49 19.79 15.1 17.8 15.1 C 15.81 15.1 14.2 13.49 14.2 11.5 C 14.2 9.51 15.81 7.9 17.8 7.9 Z
agents | F | M 9.5 13.6 C 11.49 13.6 13.1 15.21 13.1 17.2 C 13.1 19.19 11.49 20.8 9.5 20.8 C 7.51 20.8 5.9 19.19 5.9 17.2 C 5.9 15.21 7.51 13.6 9.5 13.6 Z

# ── Open Command Center ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Four panes: the ops workspace. Mirrors macOS `square.grid.2x2` exactly —
# this one needed no interpretation, it is a literal 2x2 of rounded squares.
grid | F | M 4.4 4.4 L 10.2 4.4 C 10.42 4.4 10.6 4.58 10.6 4.8 L 10.6 10.2 C 10.6 10.42 10.42 10.6 10.2 10.6 L 4.4 10.6 C 4.18 10.6 4 10.42 4 10.2 L 4 4.8 C 4 4.58 4.18 4.4 4.4 4.4 Z
grid | F | M 13.8 4.4 L 19.6 4.4 C 19.82 4.4 20 4.58 20 4.8 L 20 10.2 C 20 10.42 19.82 10.6 19.6 10.6 L 13.8 10.6 C 13.58 10.6 13.4 10.42 13.4 10.2 L 13.4 4.8 C 13.4 4.58 13.58 4.4 13.8 4.4 Z
grid | F | M 4.4 13.4 L 10.2 13.4 C 10.42 13.4 10.6 13.58 10.6 13.8 L 10.6 19.2 C 10.6 19.42 10.42 19.6 10.2 19.6 L 4.4 19.6 C 4.18 19.6 4 19.42 4 19.2 L 4 13.8 C 4 13.58 4.18 13.4 4.4 13.4 Z
grid | F | M 13.8 13.4 L 19.6 13.4 C 19.82 13.4 20 13.58 20 13.8 L 20 19.2 C 20 19.42 19.82 19.6 19.6 19.6 L 13.8 19.6 C 13.58 19.6 13.4 19.42 13.4 19.2 L 13.4 13.8 C 13.4 13.58 13.58 13.4 13.8 13.4 Z

# ── Start Stack ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Filled triangle, matching `play.fill`. Corners softened slightly so it
# does not look sharper than the stop square sitting directly beneath it.
play | F | M 7.6 4.9 C 7.6 4.3 8.25 3.94 8.76 4.25 L 19.3 11.35 C 19.77 11.65 19.77 12.35 19.3 12.65 L 8.76 19.75 C 8.25 20.06 7.6 19.7 7.6 19.1 Z

# ── Stop Stack ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Filled rounded square, matching `stop.fill`. This is the shape Segoe MDL2
# has no clean glyph for — the reason Stop was a hand-drawn rectangle on
# Windows while its neighbours were font glyphs, and why it sat visibly
# heavier than them. Owning it settles that permanently.
stop | F | M 6.6 5.4 L 17.4 5.4 C 18.06 5.4 18.6 5.94 18.6 6.6 L 18.6 17.4 C 18.6 18.06 18.06 18.6 17.4 18.6 L 6.6 18.6 C 5.94 18.6 5.4 18.06 5.4 17.4 L 5.4 6.6 C 5.4 5.94 5.94 5.4 6.6 5.4 Z

# ── Restart Stack ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Circular arrow, matching `arrow.clockwise`. The ring is deliberately open
# at the top-right so the arrowhead has somewhere to sit; a closed ring with
# a head pasted on top reads as a smudge at 16px.
refresh | S2 | M 20.2 12 C 20.2 16.53 16.53 20.2 12 20.2 C 7.47 20.2 3.8 16.53 3.8 12 C 3.8 7.47 7.47 3.8 12 3.8 C 15.1 3.8 17.8 5.52 19.2 8.06
refresh | F | M 20.6 3.4 L 20.6 9.1 C 20.6 9.38 20.38 9.6 20.1 9.6 L 14.4 9.6 C 13.96 9.6 13.74 9.07 14.05 8.76 L 19.76 3.05 C 20.07 2.74 20.6 2.96 20.6 3.4 Z

# ── Check for Updates ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Down arrow in an open ring, matching `arrow.down.circle`.
download | S2 | M 12 3.4 C 16.75 3.4 20.6 7.25 20.6 12 C 20.6 16.75 16.75 20.6 12 20.6 C 7.25 20.6 3.4 16.75 3.4 12 C 3.4 7.25 7.25 3.4 12 3.4 Z
download | S2 | M 12 7.6 L 12 15.6
download | S2 | M 8.4 12.2 L 12 15.8 L 15.6 12.2

# ── Update available ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Up arrow knocked out of a FILLED ring, matching `arrow.up.circle.fill`.
# The K subpath paints in the menu background colour, so the arrow reads as
# a hole rather than needing a second colour channel through the renderer.
update | F | M 12 3.4 C 16.75 3.4 20.6 7.25 20.6 12 C 20.6 16.75 16.75 20.6 12 20.6 C 7.25 20.6 3.4 16.75 3.4 12 C 3.4 7.25 7.25 3.4 12 3.4 Z
update | K | M 11 16.4 L 11 10.5 L 8.9 12.6 C 8.5 13 7.9 13 7.5 12.6 C 7.1 12.2 7.1 11.6 7.5 11.2 L 11.3 7.4 C 11.7 7 12.3 7 12.7 7.4 L 16.5 11.2 C 16.9 11.6 16.9 12.2 16.5 12.6 C 16.1 13 15.5 13 15.1 12.6 L 13 10.5 L 13 16.4 C 13 17 12.6 17.4 12 17.4 C 11.4 17.4 11 17 11 16.4 Z

# ── Request a Feature ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lightbulb. macOS used a literal emoji here, which is the one place the two
# platforms drifted in KIND rather than degree — an emoji is full-colour and
# font-dependent, so it never matched the monochrome items around it on
# either platform. Now it is a drawn mark like everything else.
bulb | S2 | M 12 2.8 C 15.9 2.8 19 5.9 19 9.8 C 19 12.1 17.8 13.8 16.7 15.1 C 16 15.9 15.7 16.6 15.7 17.4 L 8.3 17.4 C 8.3 16.6 8 15.9 7.3 15.1 C 6.2 13.8 5 12.1 5 9.8 C 5 5.9 8.1 2.8 12 2.8 Z
